            <ArticleTitle>Cyclic sciatica of endometriosis. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>415-416</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 27-year-old woman with right-sided cyclic sciatica and stiffness of the right hip joint, unresponsive to orthopaedic measures, is presented. An exploratory laparotomy revealed pelvic endometriosis. On oestrogen suppression therapy, she has been symptom-free for eleven months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
